  "problem": "Solve the inequality $-{(\\frac{5}{3})}^{3-4x}<{8}^{3-x}.$\n\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}\n$x\\,<\\,\\infty $",
  "worked_solution": "Since ${8}^{3-x}$ is always positive and $-{(\\frac{5}{3})}^{3-4x}$ is always negative, we always have\n\n$$\n-{(\\frac{5}{3})}^{3-4x}<{8}^{3-x}.\n$$\n\nThis means that the given inequality is satisfied by all real values of $x.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n-\\infty <x<\\infty \n$$",
